# Connect YouTube downloads — home PC Cobalt (recommended) or Render Cobalt

## Live production: Connect on Render + Cobalt on your PC

Your PC runs Cobalt (home IP). Render Connect calls it through a **Cloudflare Tunnel**.

### Step 1 — Home PC (once)

```powershell
cd E:\Connect\home-cobalt
.\install.ps1          # Cobalt auto-start on login
.\enable-live.ps1      # Turn on API auth + set public tunnel URL
```

For a **stable URL** (recommended), use a Cloudflare **named tunnel**:
1. `cloudflared tunnel login`
2. `cloudflared tunnel create connect-cobalt`
3. Copy credentials to `home-cobalt/tunnel/credentials.json`
4. Copy `tunnel/config.yml.template` → `tunnel/config.yml`, set tunnel ID + hostname
5. In `live.env` set:
   ```
   COBALT_LIVE=1
   COBALT_PUBLIC_URL=https://cobalt.yourdomain.com
   CLOUDFLARED_CONFIG=E:/Connect/home-cobalt/tunnel/config.yml
   ```
6. `pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs && pm2 save`

**Quick test only** (URL changes on restart): run `.\setup-quick-tunnel.ps1`

### Step 2 — Render Connect dashboard → Environment

```
COBALT_API_URL=https://cobalt.yourdomain.com
COBALT_API_KEY=7699759e-fe6a-49a9-9589-cc22baf0188e
YT_DL_PREFER_COBALT=true
YT_DL_COBALT_ONLY=false
YT_DL_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
YOUTUBE_COOKIES_B64=<same cookies as local>
```

Redeploy Connect after saving.

### Step 3 — Verify

```powershell
cd E:\Connect\server
node scripts/verify-home-cobalt.js https://cobalt.yourdomain.com
```

---

## Local dev only

```
COBALT_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000
COBALT_API_KEY=7699759e-fe6a-49a9-9589-cc22baf0188e
YT_DL_PREFER_COBALT=true
YT_DL_COBALT_ONLY=false
YT_DL_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
```

---

## Legacy: Render Cobalt + yt-session (optional)

Only if you do not use home PC Cobalt:

```
COBALT_API_URL=https://cobalt-yt.onrender.com
```

Requires working yt-session `/token` on Render (Standard 2GB plan).

`YT_DL_COBALT_ONLY=false` keeps yt-dlp fallback if Cobalt fails.
